<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>07 · RESULTS (6/6) — H3 AND H4</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        One question we cannot answer, one we can only describe
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 32, marginTop: 20 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 566, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '16px 20px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#FF6B6B', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>H3 · INFORMATION VERSUS ARCHITECTURE</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 6, lineHeight: 1.25 }}>
                No labelled chain-level target — so A5 is never merely unrun
            </Text>

            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', width: 524, marginTop: 14 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', background: '#16233A', padding: '8px 12px' }}>
                    <Text style={{ width: 190, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Pre-registered input</Text>
                    <Text style={{ width: 200, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>In the data?</Text>
                    <Text style={{ width: 134, fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Verdict</Text>
                </Box>
                {[
                    ['repeat-unit count', 'no such column, 18,152 rows', 'cannot inject'],
                    ['connection weight block', 'identical in all 18,036', 'zero variance'],
                    ['multi-unit sequence', 'one row per repeat unit', 'no sequence'],
                ].map(([a, b, c]) => (
                    <Box key={a} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', padding: '9px 12px', background: '#0E1728', borderBottom: '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                        <Text style={{ width: 190, fontSize: 16, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{a}</Text>
                        <Text style={{ width: 200, fontSize: 16, color: '#C3D0E2' }}>{b}</Text>
                        <Text style={{ width: 134, fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFB020' }}>{c}</Text>
                    </Box>
                ))}
            </Box>

            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#C3D0E2', marginTop: 12, lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Feeding A5 anyway would append three constant columns. Its record count is 0, its status
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020' }}> not_constructible_data_unavailable</span> — writing &quot;zero gain&quot; is forbidden.
            </Text>

            <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#93A8C2', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>
                <span style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>What we have instead:</span> a per-task noise floor.
                Median |ΔR²| 0.0046 across 8 tasks; A3 beats it on 5 of 8.
            </Text>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '16px 20px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#4D8DFF', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>H4 · CROSSOVER</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', marginTop: 6, lineHeight: 1.25 }}>
                Two properties cross; the third never does
            </Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 26, marginTop: 16 }}>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 38, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>≈ 56</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 4 }}>Tg · labels 30–355</Text>
                </Box>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 38, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#4D8DFF', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>≈ 59</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 4 }}>dielectric · 30–235</Text>
                </Box>
                <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 38, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFB020', lineHeight: 1.05 }}>none</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 4 }}>Tm · negative 30–134</Text>
                </Box>
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#C3D0E2', marginTop: 16, lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Below roughly 60 training rows the graph arm leads; above it the classical arm leads and stays ahead. That is
                &quot;Λ is mostly negative&quot;, read from the other end of the axis.
            </Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#A8B8CE', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
                Three limits, stated up front: only three properties, descriptive with no significance test, and windows of
                different width — so the two n* are not comparable with each other. Both crossings are log-n interpolations
                between the 30- and 60-row design points: read them as a bracket.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 'auto' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>
            Floor from 48 calibration runs (16 baseline, 16 constant, 16 shuffled) · crossings from 225 paired differences
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>13 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
